.TH GETLINE 3crunch "" "Crunch" "Crunch Library Manual"
.SH NAME
getline \- read a line into a dynamically sized buffer
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <stdio.h>
.PP
.BI "ssize_t getline(char** " line ", size_t* " capacity ", FILE* " stream ");"
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.BR getline ()
reads through a newline or end of file, growing the buffer with
.BR realloc (3crunch)
as needed. It includes a newline if one was read and appends a NUL byte.
The caller owns the buffer and must free it, including after an error.
Set the buffer pointer to null to request an initial allocation.
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns the number of bytes read, including a newline but excluding the
terminating NUL. Returns \-1 on error or end of file before any byte.
.SH ERRORS
.TP
.B EINVAL
An argument is null.
.TP
.B ENOMEM
The buffer could not be allocated or grown.
.TP
.B EOVERFLOW
The required buffer size exceeds the supported range.
.PP
Stream reads can report other errors.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fgetc (3crunch),
.BR realloc (3crunch)
